From: Axiado Corporation <engineering@axiado.com>
Date: 2025-01-01 00:00:00
Subject: [PATCH] ax_hal: pass CFLAGS (not CALIPTRA_C_FLAGS) to libcaliptra build

libcaliptra/Makefile compiles its objects with $(CFLAGS), but
ax_hal/CMakeLists.txt was exporting the flag string under the wrong
env-var name (CALIPTRA_C_FLAGS), so the Makefile saw nothing and built
with the arm-none-eabi default soft-float ABI. The resulting
libcaliptra.a then fails to link against the rest of bali-system.elf
(which is hard-float) with:

  ld: error: bali-system.elf uses VFP register arguments,
      .../caliptra-sw/libcaliptra/libcaliptra.a(caliptra_api.o) does not
  ld: failed to merge target specific data of file ...libcaliptra.a(...)

Three fixes in one hunk:
  * Export the value as CFLAGS so the Makefile actually picks it up.
  * Build the flag string from the same cpu/fpu/float-abi vars that
    base/r52-compile-args.cmake sets. The previous use of
    $<TARGET_PROPERTY:base_hal,COMPILE_OPTIONS> expanded to an empty
    string because base_hal inherits those flags from the directory
    scope (add_compile_options) rather than via target_compile_options.
  * Quote each "VAR=VALUE" token passed to `cmake -E env` so the
    space-separated CFLAGS value stays in a single env entry.

Upstream-Status: Pending [submitted to Axiado ax_hal develop branch]
Signed-off-by: Axiado Corporation <engineering@axiado.com>
---
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -94,14 +94,17 @@
     set(ENV{RTL_SOC_IFC_INCLUDE_PATH}
         ${LIBCALIPTRA_DIR}/../hw/1.0/rtl/src/soc_ifc/rtl
     )
+    # libcaliptra/Makefile reads $(CFLAGS). Build the flag string from the
+    # same cpu/fpu/float-abi vars the rest of bali-hal uses so the resulting
+    # libcaliptra.a is ABI-compatible (hard-float) with bali-system.elf.
     set(CALIPTRA_C_FLAGS
-        "$<JOIN:$<TARGET_PROPERTY:base_hal,COMPILE_OPTIONS>, >"
+        "-mcpu=${GCC_CPU} -mfpu=${FPU_CONFIG} -mfloat-abi=${FLOAT}"
     )
     add_custom_target(build_libcaliptra ALL
         COMMAND ${CMAKE_COMMAND} -E env
-            RTL_SOC_IFC_INCLUDE_PATH=$ENV{RTL_SOC_IFC_INCLUDE_PATH}
-            CROSS_COMPILE=${TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX}
-            CALIPTRA_C_FLAGS=${CALIPTRA_C_FLAGS}
+            "RTL_SOC_IFC_INCLUDE_PATH=$ENV{RTL_SOC_IFC_INCLUDE_PATH}"
+            "CROSS_COMPILE=${TOOLCHAIN_PREFIX}"
+            "CFLAGS=${CALIPTRA_C_FLAGS}"
             make -C ${LIBCALIPTRA_DIR}
         WORKING_DIRECTORY ${LIBCALIPTRA_DIR}
         COMMENT "Building libcaliptra with ${CALIPTRA_C_FLAGS}"

